       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "CKD (adults):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " start 50 to 100 Units/kg 3 times weekly IV or SC; IV is recommended on hemodialysis."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Correct or exclude other causes of anemia first; after starting and after each dose change, check Hb weekly until stable."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " PRCA that began after any erythropoietin product; serious allergic reaction to Epogen; multidose vials (benzyl alcohol) in neonates, infants, pregnant or lactating women."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Raises seizure risk in CKD:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " monitor closely for premonitory neurologic symptoms during the first several months. Serious allergic reactions (anaphylaxis, angioedema, bronchospasm): stop it permanently. Suspected SJS/TEN: stop it immediately."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Poor or lost Hb response:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " look for iron deficiency, infection, inflammation or bleeding, then PRCA. Severe anemia with a low retic count: withhold it and test for neutralizing antibodies. PRCA: stop permanently and don't switch to another ESA."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
